              <ToolIcon name="zap" class="w-5 h-5" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">
              The Difference Between Lossless Archival and Next-Gen Delivery
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Legacy archival formats like PNG rely on <strong>DEFLATE (LZ77 + Huffman coding)</strong> combined with five 2D predictive filter heuristics (Sub, Up, Average, Paeth). Every pixel is preserved bit-for-bit, making PNG the gold standard for software screenshots, vector diagrams, and typographic marks.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Conversely, next-generation codecs like <strong>WebP and AVIF</strong> leverage spatial prediction algorithms derived from VP8 and AV1 video standards. By predicting pixel blocks from adjacent macroblocks, they achieve 30% to 55% smaller payloads than JPEG and PNG at equivalent visual fidelity, dramatically accelerating Largest Contentful Paint (LCP).
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80">
