              <ToolIcon name="layers" class="w-5 h-5" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">
              Alpha Channel Flattening During Transparent Conversions
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
              The 24-bit JPEG and BMP file specifications have no alpha transparency channel. When converting 32-bit RGBA files (transparent PNG, WebP, or SVG) to JPEG, every pixel's alpha byte is discarded. Traditional converters assume a black background <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">#000000</code>, creating unsightly dark halos along anti-aliased edges.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              FastToolVerse implements <strong>Smart Transparency Compositing</strong>. Before running raster quantization, an offscreen canvas renders an opaque matte (defaulting to pure white <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">#FFFFFF</code> or any custom hex color) beneath the transparent pixels, ensuring silky-smooth anti-aliased edges with zero dark fringes.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-medium">Algorithm: Alpha Matte Blending (C = α·C_fg + (1-α)·C_bg)</span>
          </div>
        </article>

